That's what I do, although I do not like the approach, precisely,
because I need two turns to get at some stuff. I keep things in a(n
oilskin) sack that I might need fast and that should not be cursed.

Which brings me to a question. My main reason for keeping my bag of
holding in a sack is that there are generally (always?) two items in the
inventory that are affected by the malignant aura. Since I always check
my inventory after getting the "malignant aura" message, it would be
safe to keep the bag of holding outside the sack, if those two malignant
aura attacks cannot hit the same object, i.e. if the bag cannot go from
blessed to cursed in one turn. Then it can be reblessed immediately
after going to uncursed. Otherwise, it may be too heavy or you may lose
items when trying to retrieve holy water from it. (I usually do not
carry a wand of cancellation on the ascension run. Even if it is in a
sack, it is dangerous. I might unintentionally put the sack into the bag
rather than vice versa.)

So my question is: can an object go from blessed to cursed during one
malignant aura attack? I seem to recall that my blessed assault rifle
went to cursed immediately during a curse cast at me by Maugneshaagar
[slash'em], but I may be in error here.

